      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    .container-border1 {\r\n        border: 2px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px 50px;\r\n        padding-top: 20px;\r\n        padding-right: 20px;\r\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\r\n        padding-left: 20px;\r\n        background-color: white;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n        Do you have a single ball or skein of yarn? Want a quick scarf?\r\n        This version is a quick knit that can be worked in any stitch pattern.<br>Because of our needlebed limitations, this style is appropriate for scarves only. If you'd like a larger shawl, consider one of choices below.<br><div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n            <i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <b>TIP: </b> <em>For even faster knitting, flip this around and start with 2-3 needles and INCREASE to the widest part of the scarf.</em> Use a <a data-vimeoid=\"151858451\" class=\"videopopup\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> KISS increase</a> on the carriage side EVERY ROW.\r\n        </div>\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/60/scarf_as_worn.jpg\">\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5651,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Simple Triangle Scarf",
          "slug": "simple-triangle-scarf",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
