      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\nWith this design, the widest point of the shawl is across the shoulders. The knitting is easy with increases and decreases worked every-other-row.<br>Depending on your gauge, with this version, you can make a generous shawl that will cover your shoulders and keep you warm.<br>By starting at a point, horizontal stripes or stitch patterns will run vertically as the shawl is worn.<br>Get creative!  Use stripes, mix 'n match stitch patterns ... you are the designer!\r\n\r\n\t<img src=\"/path/images/158/to-the-point_as_worn.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
