    {
      "title": "Chevron",
      "slug": "chevron",
      "displayOrder": 5,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 391,
        "lessonOrder": 5
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\tThis 2-piece design, knit with horizontal stripes or stitch patterns, creates a lovely chevron shape at the center back. Because it's knit in 2 pieces, you shouldn't run into any needlebed limitations and you can make it any size you like!<br>\r\nUnlike the other versions in this collection, to keep the proportions correct, the shaping is worked according to the Magic Formula (not every-other-row).<br>\r\n\r\n\t\t<em><i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><b>TIP:</b><br> To match the chevron color repeats, be sure to reverse the shaping. Start one piece on the far left of the needlebed working the increases and decreases on the right. Knit the other piece by starting on the far right of the needlebed and work the shaping on the left.\r\n\t\t</em><br>\r\n\t\r\n\t<img src=\"/path/images/158/chevron_version_text.jpg\">\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5624,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
